WEBVTT

00:00:03.250 --> 00:00:15.583
Hi, I'm Muhammad Husain Aboutalebi, an AI specialist, Mechanical Engineer, and Full-Stack Software Engineer. Today, I'm walking you through the core of my scalable, microservices platform.

00:00:15.583 --> 00:00:32.983
We start at the infrastructure level. Using Docker Compose, I'm orchestrating the entire containerized architecture. A quick check confirms that all our isolated services—including our PostgreSQL databases and Go backends—are up and running perfectly.

00:00:32.983 --> 00:00:53.366
For the Authentication Microservice, I use grpcurl to demonstrate gRPC server reflection. This dynamically exposes our protocol buffer definitions and endpoints. It proves the API contract is clean, strict, and instantly discoverable by client applications.

00:00:58.566 --> 00:01:15.633
Next, we move to execution. Using the Bruno API client, I trigger a gRPC user registration request. Switching over to pgAdmin, you can see the new user data is successfully and securely persisted in our PostgreSQL database.

00:01:35.383 --> 00:01:45.983
Finally, I validate the authentication tokens to confirm that our JWT security boundaries and gRPC interceptors are fully operational.

00:01:57.700 --> 00:02:03.400
This workflow represents a production-ready, highly decoupled backend architecture.

00:02:03.400 --> 00:02:04.966
Thanks for watching!